# Frontend Design Standards

- Build production-quality, modern SaaS interfaces.
- Avoid generic AI-generated dashboard designs.
- Use Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui.
- Prefer clean layouts, consistent spacing and visual hierarchy.
- Use Lucide icons instead of emojis.
- Use subtle borders, shadows and hover transitions.
- Use consistent typography and a professional colour palette.
- Support desktop, tablet and mobile screens.
- Ensure proper loading, empty, error and success states.
- Use accessible components and keyboard navigation.
- Avoid unnecessary gradients and excessive rounded cards.
- Use charts and meaningful visualisations where appropriate.
- Reuse existing components instead of duplicating UI.
- Keep components modular and maintainable.

Before implementation:
1. Review the existing design system.
2. Identify reusable components.
3. Plan the page layout.
4. Implement the UI.
5. Run the application and inspect the actual browser rendering.
6. Refine spacing, alignment, responsiveness and visual consistency.
